      "id": 1,
      "text": "Skillman takes its name from the Skillman family.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skillman%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When railroad officials socialized at a nearby Skillman home, the new station was named for the family.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skillman%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened at the station, and a small village with a hay press, feed store and hardware store sprouted around it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skillman%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Although the train station is gone, remnants of the village still exist where Camp Meeting Avenue meets Skillman Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skillman%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Skillman postal address covers an area much larger than the CDP, serving about half of Montgomery Township.",
